A||||2||Dan010||Can you flood a 2.8?||||1||
Z||000000||Dan010||12-07-2001||11:01 PM||||While replacing the front end components,<BR>I would turn the ingition key on and off to un-lock the steering wheel, did this 5 or 6 times in a 3 hour period, each time the fuel pump would start. after finishing, tryed to start her up, had to crank a quite few times before firing, usually fires right off.<BR>Is this normal????<BR>Or there something leaking???<P>Thanks <BR>Dan ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-07-2001||11:08 PM||||You shouldn't have any problems with just turning the key on and off.  The fuel that is pressurized and sent to the fuel rail will just drain back into the tank.<P>However, if you were cranking it over and it wouldn't start then yes, it is possible to flood the engine.<P>From what you described I don't think you have anything to worry about.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fastback87||12-07-2001||11:15 PM||||I could be you have leaking injectors, so when you pressurize the system there is some fuel leaking into the cylinder causing it to act flooded...Just my 2 cents||||reg||1
